trength, corresponding to an induced target δyt . For p-loss, the gradient scales with py (slope for Non-observed token k depends on py). Therefore, its gradient is near-zero when py ≈ 0, and the target probability is the same as current probability (Q = p); the induced target approaches δyt only when py → 1, where the model is certain. An interactive plot is available on our project page.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11189v1-Figure3-1-d30eea8e969b.png","asset_sha256":"d30eea8e969bd9c42956cf796ade379f3a911310677c686b21b6a1040355128d","metadata_sha256":"053831eb1555fa4d14b101b7e4d9f8467cf42e47fce92a2e50c81cd2aae8f285"},{"artifact_id":"Table6","kind":"table","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"09a8f748630f01b8d2dd070b7bc14aec3148eb251c1f425d4d0c2ab18a7f287a","page_index":18,"region":{"x1":108.96,"y1":230.4,"x2":503.04,"y2":394.08},"caption_region":{"x1":107.6709976196289,"y1":210.68453979492188,"x2":503.9953918457031,"y2":227.59600830078125},"caption":"Table 6: Ablation Study. Average@16 accuracy using Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B trained on NuminaMath (top) and OpenR1 (bottom) to ablate on two key designs of the method.","image_text":["c","=","0.2","22.09","23.23","5.00","33.44","58.24","28.48","c","=","0.5","29.54","33.19","11.67","50.47","70.71","39.10","c","=","1.0","22.27","27.26","8.14","41.72","60.32","31.82","TARGET-SFT","33.09","34.84","13.13","51.72","72.38","41.24","Constant","branch","c,","instead","of","residual","1","−","γt","Distill","(c","=","0.2)","13.99","13.08","1.45","17.34","44.32","18.33","Distill","(c","=","0.5)","19.13","18.94","4.16","26.56","53.81","24.92","Distill","(c","=","0.8)","25.46","23.64","6.68","37.50","60.92","30.83","Distill","(c","=","1.0)","18.07","18.49","4.38","28.28","45.22","22.81","TARGET-SFT","(η","=","0.2)","27.41","29.48","9.17","44.06","65.96","35.16","TARGET-SFT","(η","=","0.5)","32.20","31.59","8.96","47.03","70.20","38.05","T